 - [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
 - [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
 - [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When a valid snapshot import completes validation, the system SHALL build a new SQLite index file in a single transaction and atomically activate it by renaming the database file.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When the active SQLite database file is corrupt or missing, the system SHALL fall back to the previous snapshot's database file and report the fallback.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: When a lookup executes, the system SHALL return a result within 250 ms on kiosk hardware with 4 GB RAM.
+- [ ] **REG-008**: When a snapshot import is in progress, the system SHALL allow concurrent read-only lookups against the previously active snapshot without blocking.
+- [ ] **REG-009**: When a snapshot import is interrupted, the system SHALL clean up any partial database file on the next import attempt.
